+### 6.1 The radius reading, recorded (lead, 2026-09-03, S48-1a correction round 2)
+
+`G48-4`'s negative arc probe ran on `1×1 at the rounded corner` against the suite's Chromium (`#dsh-frame` border 1 px, `border-radius` 14 px, padding-box radius 13): a probe at 14.5 px from the arc centre and a diagonal sweep over the whole window between the padding-box curve and the frame's literal square corner (13 → 19.8 px) return the `nw` handle at every sample; the first point that stops returning it is the frame's own rectangular corner, which resolves to `#dsh-stage`. **The reading is the third of the three values named above: the browser clips descendant hit-testing to the padding-box RECTANGLE and not to its `border-radius` curve.** The full trail is in the S48-1a correction-round-2 executor report.
+
+This is the branch §6 already prices — "the reachable surface at a rounded corner is larger than §2 says and the probe-point rule loosens accordingly" — so it is an expected Evidence Gate result, not a stop for replanning, and the lead applied it as follows. **Production is untouched**: the module never computed the clip under the new model; the browser does, and it does so with a rectangle. **The oracles drop the arc**: the reachable surface is the measured rect intersected with the padding-box rectangle of the frame and the ring layer; `arcsOf`'s promotion in §2.1 and its 1 px re-derivation are void, and the arc-aware reading in `G48-4` becomes the rect-aware one, with the per-handle split on the three small fixtures re-run and RECORDED under the rectangle. §2's sentence "a `border-radius` on that ancestor clips to the rounded shape" is false for hit-testing and superseded by this section; the sentence stands as written above as the record of what the plan assumed. **The measurement itself stays in the suite** as a standing row asserting the reading, so that a browser change which starts clipping hits to the curve shows up as that row going RED with a name rather than as unexplained reachable-surface failures elsewhere. The pre-mortem's "Residual" on this premise is thereby discharged.
+
+The one user-visible consequence — a handle region that reaches past the painted curve into the frame's rounded-off corner is grabbable where nothing is painted, on the four frame corners only and within a 13 px radius — is recorded here as the cost of the ruling, priced against the alternative (writing an intersected rect onto the node, rejected in §2 for sliding the chip inward), and left as is.
+
+**Two more sentences above are superseded by the same measurement and stand only as the record of the assumption.** In `G48-4`'s assignment, "`1×1 at the rounded corner` — the four bands clear the clip entirely at the measured padding-box radius, so they take the fallback" and "its corners are 14.1 to 15.6 px from that centre, so every one of them is outside the clip and a press there reaches nothing" are both false under the rectangle: on that fixture all eight handles are reachable and the canonical-owner probe at the box corner resolves. The fixture stays in the row as the layer-origin and quantisation case, not as a "clip rects diverge" case, and `FRAME_CORNER_RADIUS_PX`'s "where the two clip rects diverge" gloss is likewise void (the constant is read only by the lab and goes in `S48-1b`; its value, 12, was never re-measured against the shipped `rounded-xl`, which the reading put at 14).
+
+**One record was written early.** EG-1's reorder-armable residue reading — including the live arming attempt at `rfcol3 @ 8px` — was measured in `S48-1a` and its tracker paragraph was written there, in the docs commit that accompanies the model commit, because the measurement and its record are the same evidence and splitting them would have made `S48-2` transcribe a report. `S48-2`'s record scope is reduced by exactly that paragraph: it still writes EG-1's alternate-path (b) record and the `| B-Q5 |` row's shares; it does not rewrite the reorder residue.
+
 ## 7. Story sequence, and where a commit cannot be green
 
 **`S48-0` — declare the superseded rulings. Docs only.** This phase reverses TWO written rulings, and they are declared separately because they are different KINDS of reversal: one ruling's subject stopped existing, the other's is alive and the reversal is a priced decision. Collapsing them into one paragraph would let the second borrow the first's mootness argument, which is exactly the move that makes a paid cost look free.
