 ## BUG-7 — JIT preview `<style>` leaked Tailwind preflight+theme globally — RESOLVED (2026-07-08, `ceca1a1`)
 User-reported: entering the chip editor for a container-with-className, then editing a chip and clicking the empty chip-field / completing via the dropdown, corrupted the page (fonts changed, black borders on some containers) — transient, self-healed on leaving the chip-add-input. **Root cause:** Tailwind v4 `build()` emits a FULL stylesheet (candidate utilities + `@layer base` preflight + `@layer theme` `:root` vars); the live-preview injected the whole thing into the global `<style id="dsh-preview-jit">`, leaking the reset (fonts/`border:0 solid`/box-sizing) across the page while a novel-token preview was live (cleared → "transient"). The seam's docstring even wrongly CLAIMED "only carries utility rules". **Fix:** `stripPreviewGlobals()` brace-matches + removes the `@layer base`/`@layer theme` blocks before injection — the preview is now an additive utility DELTA; candidates resolve `var(--*)` from the live page `:root`. Trade-off: previewing a theme color the app never statically uses shows no color (graceful). Real-compiler smoke + pure unit tests + live Playwright (p-[13px] injects the util, zero leak, html font unchanged). descvi 1082 green; screens.json byte-identical.
 
